     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 3, \"rationale\": \"The target is an OR of h3_0, h3_1 and h3_2, so all three must be cut. Two blocks are not enough. Stopping h3_2 needs either h3_2 itself blocked, or both h1_2 and h2_2. If h1_2 and h2_2 are blocked, h2_1 is still reached via h1_0, so h3_1 is reached. If h3_2 is blocked, one more block cannot stop both h3_1 and h3_0: h3_1 needs itself blocked or all of h1_2, h2_2 and h2_1, and neither choice also stops h3_0. Three blocks work, for example {h3_0, h3_1, h3_2}, or {h1_0, h1_2, h2_2}, which stops h3_0 (AND), h2_1, h3_1 and h3_2.\"}"
    }
